     "algorithm": "This algorithm selects the next node by maximizing a combined score that positively weights normalized betweenness and core number to emphasize nodes critical for connectivity, while penalizing eigenvector centrality and clustering to avoid nodes well embedded in stable clusters, using different weights than the original.",
     "code": "def select_next_node(graph, unvisited_nodes):\n    eps = 1e-9\n    \n    degrees = [graph.nodes[n]['degree'] for n in unvisited_nodes]\n    cores = [graph.nodes[n]['core_number'] for n in unvisited_nodes]\n    clusts = [graph.nodes[n]['clustering'] for n in unvisited_nodes]\n    eigs = [graph.nodes[n]['eigenvector'] for n in unvisited_nodes]\n    betws = [graph.nodes[n]['betweenness'] for n in unvisited_nodes]\n\n    def norm(vals):\n        mn, mx = min(vals), max(vals)\n        if mx - mn < eps:\n            return [0.5]*len(vals)\n        return [(v - mn) / (mx - mn) for v in vals]\n\n    core_n = norm(cores)\n    betw_n = norm(betws)\n    eig_n = norm(eigs)\n    clust_n = norm(clusts)\n\n    best_score = -float('inf')\n    best_node = None\n\n    for i, n in enumerate(unvisited_nodes):\n        # new score = (betw_norm * core_norm) - 0.7 * (eig_norm + clust_norm)\n        score = (betw_n[i] * core_n[i]) - 0.7 * (eig_n[i] + clust_n[i])\n        if score > best_score:\n            best_score = score\n            best_node = n\n\n    return best_node",
